# Next.js Rules

## App Router
- Use `'use client'` directive for client components
- Use server components when possible for better performance
- Follow Next.js App Router conventions
- Use `next/link` for navigation
- Implement proper SEO with metadata

## File Structure
- Use `page.tsx` for route pages
- Use `layout.tsx` for shared layouts
- Use `loading.tsx` for loading states
- Use `error.tsx` for error boundaries
- Use `not-found.tsx` for 404 pages

## Server vs Client Components
```typescript
// Server Component (default)
export default async function PokemonDetailPage({ 
  params 
}: { 
  params: { name: string } 
}) {
  const pokemon = await getPokemonDetails(params.name);
  return <PokemonDetail pokemon={pokemon} />;
}

// Client Component
'use client';
export default function PokemonCard({ pokemon }: { pokemon: Pokemon }) {
  const [isHovered, setIsHovered] = useState(false);
  // Client-side logic here
}
```

## Data Fetching
- Use server components for initial data fetching
- Use client components for interactive features
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Use `loading.tsx` for loading states

## SEO & Metadata
```typescript
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Pokemon Detail',
  description: 'Detailed information about the Pokemon',
  openGraph: {
    title: 'Pokemon Detail',
    description: 'Detailed information about the Pokemon',
    images: ['/pokemon-image.jpg'],
  },
};
```

## Avoid
- Don't use client components for static content
- Don't forget to handle loading and error states
- Don't use `useEffect` for data fetching in server components
- Don't ignore SEO best practices